rem Summation of a Modular Formula
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=717

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Nn integer = 10 ** 7

rem By Fermat, b = 2^(2^p) mod p is
rem 2^(2^p mod (p-1)) mod p. Halving
rem mod p gives h with 2h = b; then
rem w = h 2^p mod p^2 equals b + p g
rem with g the wanted residue.
Pr = (Nn - 1) primesieve
Ps = (Pr array) drop 1
Ae = 2 Ps (Ps - 1) powmod
Bb = 2 Ae Ps powmod
Hh = Bb * ((Ps + 1) // 2) mod Ps
Qq = Ps * Ps
Tw = 2 Ps Qq powmod
Ww = Hh * Tw mod Qq
Dl = (Ww - Bb) mod Qq
Gg = Dl // Ps
Answer = Gg sum
Answer print
